{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause proven per /rebar-debug (fast path): NOT gh itself. Agent harnesses on this dev host export command-scope git config via env (GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=2, GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=safe.bareRepository, GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=explicit, GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1=credential.interactive, GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1=never). The bridge harness helpers git()/bare_git() in tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py inherit os.environ, so the injected safe.bareRepository=explicit fails the verification call 'git -C <bare tickets-origin.git> show tickets:bridge-event.txt' with 'fatal: cannot use bare repository'. CI exports no such vars -> green. Discriminating experiment: unsetting only GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_*/VALUE_* flips all 5 matrix params to PASS on the same tree. Sibling sweep found the same class in tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py and tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_runner_install_paths_heldout.py (21 failures total on this host). Fix (test-only): scrub GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_*/VALUE_*/PARAMETERS in the harness git helpers + runner_env, pin GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null + GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 for helper calls, and monkeypatch the hostile injection into the matrix test so the regression is deterministic in CI. RED: strengthened matrix test fails against unfixed harness in a clean env. GREEN: 45 tests pass across all 4 bridge files on this hostile host. Mutation check: symlinking gh into fake_bin still fails the test (gh hold-out contract intact). Gates: make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0. Pushed as Gerrit change 2150 (commit 71598c097c)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787463651801061001,"uuid":"655c45b6-3908-4853-a5d1-a3785891c142"}